+# Agentic Rollback & Backup Runbook
+
+Overview
+- When an agent step causes an unexpected or unsafe change, the operator must inspect stored backups (created pre-execution), perform rollback, and run postmortem.
+
+1) Identify the AgentAction
+- Use alerts or list recent AgentAction CRs:
+  kubectl -n <ns> get agentactions
+  kubectl -n <ns> get agentaction <name> -o yaml
+
+2) Find backups
+- AgentAction.status/backups contains backup URIs (s3://... or file://...). Copy the backup payload locally:
+  aws s3 cp s3://bucket/agent_backups/<...> /tmp/backup.json
+
+3) Rollback common cases
+- Deployment image change:
+  kubectl -n <ns> apply -f /tmp/backup.json
+- Replica count:
+  kubectl -n <ns> scale deployment/<name> --replicas=<previous>
+
+4) Clear circuit breaker (after remediation)
+- Run:
+  ./ops/agent/run_clear_circuit.sh <namespace>
+
+5) Postmortem & update policies
+- Add entry to incidents tracker, attach S3 evidence and AgentAction CR YAML.
+- Consider tightening safe_policy.json constraints or requiring manual approval for the action in future.
+
+6) Escalation
+- If rollback fails or production is degraded, page SRE and Security teams per on-call roster.
+
